CoBRA implements this idea through a closed-loop system that uses classic social science experiments as calibration tasks to continuously measure agents’ cognitive biases and adjust their behavior until on target.


Page 12:

￼

COBRA has two components. The first one is the classic experiment testbed for measuring the cognitive bias. The testbed currently covers 4 types of cognitive bias, each with two classic experimental paradigms. By the way, we are also building an open human study bench, which is open for contributions and collaborations. If you are interested in this part, just pin me anytime for a quick chat.

Page 13:
￼
Behavioral Regulation Engine aligns the agent’s behavior to a chosen bias level, using different calibration methods and covering all three intervention spaces of an LLM—prompt for input space, representation engineering for activations space, and fine-tuning for parameter space.

Detailed methodology for each control space is detailed in the paper, and the code is open-sourced.

